hinim/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PSPTorchinim/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PSPTorchinim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PSPTorchinim/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PSPTorchinim","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PSPTorchinim/micros/commits/ac41fa592960316daafa4f1a47edcae88901324c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-17T21:22:26Z","email":"47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Hubert Troć"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-17T21:22:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"R2603-1 into production (#541)\n\n* Reject user-to-company addition and hide users section when company does not exist (#366)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Throw AppException when adding users to a company that doesn''t exist\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Hide users section on company page when no company is created\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix: expired token triggers logout instead of surfacing 401 \"security stamp changed\" (#368)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix: logout on expired/old token instead of showing 401 security stamp error\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 248: Useless upcast\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 247: Generic catch clause\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in auth-provider.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Updated .Net packages (#371)\n\n* Updated .Net packages\n\n* Fix build error: replace removed SetDbStatementForText with custom redacting processor (#372)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix CS1061: remove SetDbStatementForText removed in SqlClient 1.15.1, add SqlQueryTextRedactingProcessor\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add GitHub issue template for AI-powered company field detection (human-in-the-loop) (#369)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add Company Types with International Support feature\n\n- Add CompanyType MongoDB entity models (CompanyType, CompanyTypeTranslation, CompanyTypeField, CompanyTypeFieldTranslation, CompanyTypeFieldOption, CompanyTypeFieldOptionTranslation)\n- Extend Brand entity with CompanyTypeId (Guid?) and CompanyTypeData (string?) for dynamic fields\n- Add MongoDB-backed CompanyTypeRepository with CRUD and country-filter operations\n- Add CompanyTypeService with GetByCountry, GetWithFields, Create, Update, AddField, UpdateFieldTranslations, Delete operations plus localisation fallback\n- Add public CompanyTypesController (GET /api/v1/CompanyTypes, GET /api/v1/CompanyTypes/{id}/fields)\n- Add AdminCompanyTypesController (SuperOwner role: POST/PUT/DELETE types and fields)\n- Add CompanyType DTOs (CompanyTypeDTO, CompanyTypeWithFieldsDTO, CreateCompanyTypeDTO, etc.)\n- Update CompanyDTO/UpdateCompanyDTO with CompanyTypeId and CompanyTypeData\n- Update CompanyService to persist/return CompanyTypeId and CompanyTypeData\n- Update BrandScope DI to register CompanyTypeRepository and CompanyTypeService\n- Update Program.cs to configure MongoDB alongside existing SQL Server\n- Update SeedData to seed initial company types (US LLC, US C-Corp, DE GmbH, FR SAS, GB Ltd)\n- Add SQL migration AddCompanyTypeFields for Brand entity changes\n- Add NotFound and CompanyTypeNotFound exception codes to ExceptionCodes\n- Add 14 new unit tests for CompanyTypeService (33 total, all passing)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Extract supported language codes to shared constant in CompanyTypeService\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add external API sync for company type field definitions\n\n- Add IExternalCompanyTypeApiClient / ExternalCompanyTypeApiClient using IHttpClientFactory\n  with a named HTTP client (timeout configured at registration) and per-request headers\n- Add ExternalCompanyTypeDefinition, ExternalCompanyTypeFieldDefinition, CompanyTypeSyncResultDTO models\n- Add SyncFromExternalApiAsync to ICompanyTypeService / CompanyTypeService: upserts company\n  types (matched by code+countryCode) fetched from external API into MongoDB\n- Add POST /v1/AdminCompanyTypes/sync?countryCode= admin endpoint (SuperOwner role)\n- Register named HTTP client with 30s timeout in BrandScope\n- Add 4 unit tests for sync functionality (37 total, all passing)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Integrate GLEIF public API as external company-types data source\n\n- ExternalCompanyTypeApiClient now calls the GLEIF entity-legal-forms API\n  (https://api.gleif.org/api/v1/entity-legal-forms) — free, no auth required, ISO 20275 codes\n- Maps GLEIF JSON:API response to ExternalCompanyTypeDefinition; filters inactive forms;\n  guarantees English translation fallback; normalises ISO 639-2/T 3-letter language codes\n- KnownRegistrationFields static class encodes required registration fields (EIN, HRB,\n  SIRET, Companies House, KvK, Firmenbuchnummer, UID) for US/DE/FR/GB/NL/AT/CH\n- BrandScope configures named HTTP client with GLEIF base URL and JSON:API Accept header\n- 19 new tests: HTTP layer mapping, inactive filtering, language normalisation,\n  KnownRegistrationFields per-country assertions (56 total, all passing)\n- Fix AT Firmenbuchnummer regex to accept upper and lowercase letters\n- Fix CH SARL entity type code (SARL not SÀRL)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add Poland (PL) to KnownRegistrationFields with NIP, KRS, REGON, address fields\n\n- GetPlFields covers Sp. z o.o., S.A. (with shareCapital), Sp. k., Sp. j., P.S.A.\n- NIP regex accepts 10-digit bare and both hyphenated formats (XXX-XXX-XX-XX / XXX-XX-XX-XXX)\n- KRS: 10-digit, REGON: 9 or 14 digits\n- LocalisedField helper adds PL translation alongside EN/DE/FR for Polish fields\n- BilingualField renamed to BaseField for non-PL jurisdictions\n- 10 new tests (66 total)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add company type admin UI with configuration page and JSON dataset import\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Merge releases/R2603: update .NET packages, upgrade MongoDB to 3.7.0, add SqlQueryTextRedactingProcessor\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix merge conflict in CompanyAPI.csproj\n\nRemoved merge conflict markers from CompanyAPI.csproj.\n\n* Add GitHub issue template for AI-powered company field detection\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in CompanyTypeAdminBlock/index.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix code scanning security alerts: remove exception message exposure, add file size limit\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix log injection (CWE-117): use StringHelper.SanitizeForLog in cache service, external API client, and company type service\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix remaining CodeQL alerts: NoOpCacheService log injection + useless upcasts in tests\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add CodeQL scanning on release branches with automatic issue creation (#376)\n\n* Automate GitHub issue creation from Grafana log alerts (Production only) (#374)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add workflow to auto-create GitHub issues from Grafana alerts\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: restrict Grafana issue creation to Production environment only\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: add Grafana alerting contact point as provisioning code\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: resolve shellcheck SC2016 and SC2129 in create-issue-from-grafana workflow\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: use PIPELINE_PAT secret for Grafana webhook authorization\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: add PIPELINE_PAT and GITHUB_REPO env vars to docker-compose and deploy pipeline\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* CodeQL scan: consolidate all alerts into a single summary issue (#528)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Consolidate CodeQL alerts into a single summary issue\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix generic catch clause in AuthService.cs (CodeQL cs/catch-of-all-exceptions) (#452)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix generic catch clause in AuthService.cs (CodeQL cs/catch-of-all-exceptions)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: auto-create release → production PR on the 24th of each month (#531)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add workflow to auto-create release-to-production PR on 24th of each month\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: skip PR creation if previous release branch not merged into production\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix CodeQL security scan findings from release branch scan (#532)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix CodeQL security findings: static-field-written-by-instance, local-not-disposed, useless-upcast, unused-local-variable, comparison-between-incompatible-types\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Combine duplicate catch blocks in UseDatabase.cs using exception filter\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: restrict CodeQL scan to production branch only (#536)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: restrict CodeQL scan to production branch only\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix CodeQL security scan findings (warnings + notes) (#534)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix CodeQL security scan findings: local-not-disposed, useless-upcast, nested-if, complex-condition, catch-all-exceptions\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: automate release PR lifecycle (Copilot review, resolve comments, branch management) (#538)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add release PR automation workflow\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: reply @copilot fix to each open review thread before marking resolved\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add commitlint to enforce Conventional Commits on PRs and local commits (#540)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add commitlint for conventional commits enforcement\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 273: Generic catch clause\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ci): remove commitlint from PR validation, enforce only via git hook (#542)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* fix(ci): skip commit lint for release-to-production PRs\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ci): remove commitlint from PR validation, enforce only via git hook\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(husky): add shebang and executable bit to commit-msg and pre-commit hooks\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b29fde5ee79a5e406bdf3edae95b0e49a0f5e013","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PSPTorchinim/micros/git/trees/b29fde5ee79a5e406bdf3edae95b0e49a0f5e013"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PSPTorchinim/micros/git/commits/ac41fa592960316daafa4f1a47edcae88901324c","verification":{"payload":"tree b29fde5ee79a5e406bdf3edae95b0e49a0f5e013\nparent 850a398f521920a2e4dc7fc5649dc8ce36734516\nauthor Hubert Troć <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com> 1773782546 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773782546 +0100\n\nR2603-1 into production (#541)\n\n* Reject user-to-company addition and hide users section when company does not exist (#366)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Throw AppException when adding users to a company that doesn''t exist\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Hide users section on company page when no company is created\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix: expired token triggers logout instead of surfacing 401 \"security stamp changed\" (#368)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix: logout on expired/old token instead of showing 401 security stamp error\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 248: Useless upcast\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 247: Generic catch clause\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in auth-provider.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Updated .Net packages (#371)\n\n* Updated .Net packages\n\n* Fix build error: replace removed SetDbStatementForText with custom redacting processor (#372)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix CS1061: remove SetDbStatementForText removed in SqlClient 1.15.1, add SqlQueryTextRedactingProcessor\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add GitHub issue template for AI-powered company field detection (human-in-the-loop) (#369)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add Company Types with International Support feature\n\n- Add CompanyType MongoDB entity models (CompanyType, CompanyTypeTranslation, CompanyTypeField, CompanyTypeFieldTranslation, CompanyTypeFieldOption, CompanyTypeFieldOptionTranslation)\n- Extend Brand entity with CompanyTypeId (Guid?) and CompanyTypeData (string?) for dynamic fields\n- Add MongoDB-backed CompanyTypeRepository with CRUD and country-filter operations\n- Add CompanyTypeService with GetByCountry, GetWithFields, Create, Update, AddField, UpdateFieldTranslations, Delete operations plus localisation fallback\n- Add public CompanyTypesController (GET /api/v1/CompanyTypes, GET /api/v1/CompanyTypes/{id}/fields)\n- Add AdminCompanyTypesController (SuperOwner role: POST/PUT/DELETE types and fields)\n- Add CompanyType DTOs (CompanyTypeDTO, CompanyTypeWithFieldsDTO, CreateCompanyTypeDTO, etc.)\n- Update CompanyDTO/UpdateCompanyDTO with CompanyTypeId and CompanyTypeData\n- Update CompanyService to persist/return CompanyTypeId and CompanyTypeData\n- Update BrandScope DI to register CompanyTypeRepository and CompanyTypeService\n- Update Program.cs to configure MongoDB alongside existing SQL Server\n- Update SeedData to seed initial company types (US LLC, US C-Corp, DE GmbH, FR SAS, GB Ltd)\n- Add SQL migration AddCompanyTypeFields for Brand entity changes\n- Add NotFound and CompanyTypeNotFound exception codes to ExceptionCodes\n- Add 14 new unit tests for CompanyTypeService (33 total, all passing)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Extract supported language codes to shared constant in CompanyTypeService\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add external API sync for company type field definitions\n\n- Add IExternalCompanyTypeApiClient / ExternalCompanyTypeApiClient using IHttpClientFactory\n  with a named HTTP client (timeout configured at registration) and per-request headers\n- Add ExternalCompanyTypeDefinition, ExternalCompanyTypeFieldDefinition, CompanyTypeSyncResultDTO models\n- Add SyncFromExternalApiAsync to ICompanyTypeService / CompanyTypeService: upserts company\n  types (matched by code+countryCode) fetched from external API into MongoDB\n- Add POST /v1/AdminCompanyTypes/sync?countryCode= admin endpoint (SuperOwner role)\n- Register named HTTP client with 30s timeout in BrandScope\n- Add 4 unit tests for sync functionality (37 total, all passing)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Integrate GLEIF public API as external company-types data source\n\n- ExternalCompanyTypeApiClient now calls the GLEIF entity-legal-forms API\n  (https://api.gleif.org/api/v1/entity-legal-forms) — free, no auth required, ISO 20275 codes\n- Maps GLEIF JSON:API response to ExternalCompanyTypeDefinition; filters inactive forms;\n  guarantees English translation fallback; normalises ISO 639-2/T 3-letter language codes\n- KnownRegistrationFields static class encodes required registration fields (EIN, HRB,\n  SIRET, Companies House, KvK, Firmenbuchnummer, UID) for US/DE/FR/GB/NL/AT/CH\n- BrandScope configures named HTTP client with GLEIF base URL and JSON:API Accept header\n- 19 new tests: HTTP layer mapping, inactive filtering, language normalisation,\n  KnownRegistrationFields per-country assertions (56 total, all passing)\n- Fix AT Firmenbuchnummer regex to accept upper and lowercase letters\n- Fix CH SARL entity type code (SARL not SÀRL)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add Poland (PL) to KnownRegistrationFields with NIP, KRS, REGON, address fields\n\n- GetPlFields covers Sp. z o.o., S.A. (with shareCapital), Sp. k., Sp. j., P.S.A.\n- NIP regex accepts 10-digit bare and both hyphenated formats (XXX-XXX-XX-XX / XXX-XX-XX-XXX)\n- KRS: 10-digit, REGON: 9 or 14 digits\n- LocalisedField helper adds PL translation alongside EN/DE/FR for Polish fields\n- BilingualField renamed to BaseField for non-PL jurisdictions\n- 10 new tests (66 total)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add company type admin UI with configuration page and JSON dataset import\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Merge releases/R2603: update .NET packages, upgrade MongoDB to 3.7.0, add SqlQueryTextRedactingProcessor\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix merge conflict in CompanyAPI.csproj\n\nRemoved merge conflict markers from CompanyAPI.csproj.\n\n* Add GitHub issue template for AI-powered company field detection\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting in CompanyTypeAdminBlock/index.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix code scanning security alerts: remove exception message exposure, add file size limit\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix log injection (CWE-117): use StringHelper.SanitizeForLog in cache service, external API client, and company type service\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix remaining CodeQL alerts: NoOpCacheService log injection + useless upcasts in tests\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add CodeQL scanning on release branches with automatic issue creation (#376)\n\n* Automate GitHub issue creation from Grafana log alerts (Production only) (#374)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add workflow to auto-create GitHub issues from Grafana alerts\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: restrict Grafana issue creation to Production environment only\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: add Grafana alerting contact point as provisioning code\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: resolve shellcheck SC2016 and SC2129 in create-issue-from-grafana workflow\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: use PIPELINE_PAT secret for Grafana webhook authorization\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: add PIPELINE_PAT and GITHUB_REPO env vars to docker-compose and deploy pipeline\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* CodeQL scan: consolidate all alerts into a single summary issue (#528)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Consolidate CodeQL alerts into a single summary issue\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix generic catch clause in AuthService.cs (CodeQL cs/catch-of-all-exceptions) (#452)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix generic catch clause in AuthService.cs (CodeQL cs/catch-of-all-exceptions)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: auto-create release → production PR on the 24th of each month (#531)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add workflow to auto-create release-to-production PR on 24th of each month\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: skip PR creation if previous release branch not merged into production\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix CodeQL security scan findings from release branch scan (#532)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix CodeQL security findings: static-field-written-by-instance, local-not-disposed, useless-upcast, unused-local-variable, comparison-between-incompatible-types\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Combine duplicate catch blocks in UseDatabase.cs using exception filter\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: restrict CodeQL scan to production branch only (#536)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: restrict CodeQL scan to production branch only\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix CodeQL security scan findings (warnings + notes) (#534)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix CodeQL security scan findings: local-not-disposed, useless-upcast, nested-if, complex-condition, catch-all-exceptions\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat: automate release PR lifecycle (Copilot review, resolve comments, branch management) (#538)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add release PR automation workflow\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: reply @copilot fix to each open review thread before marking resolved\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add commitlint to enforce Conventional Commits on PRs and local commits (#540)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: add commitlint for conventional commits enforcement\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Potential fix for code scanning alert no. 273: Generic catch clause\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot Autofix powered by AI <62310815+github-advanced-security[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ci): remove commitlint from PR validation, enforce only via git hook (#542)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* fix(ci): skip commit lint for release-to-production PRs\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(ci): remove commitlint from PR validation, enforce only via git hook\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(husky): add shebang and executable bit to commit-msg and pre-commit hooks\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-a