agement template rendering\n\nThis will help identify where the /roles-management page is failing to load.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix AutoMapper exception in GetRole - map first element instead of list\n\nFixed AutoMapper error \"Missing type map configuration or unsupported mapping. Mapping types: List`1 -> GetRoleDTO\"\n\nThe repository Get method returns List<Role>, but we were trying to map the entire list to GetRoleDTO (a single object). Changed to map req.First() instead of req to correctly map a single Role entity to GetRoleDTO.\n\n✅ All 9 role tests passing\n✅ Backend builds successfully\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix permissions not loading in roles list - include permissions in GetRoles\n\nThe roles list was showing \"0 permissions\" because GetRoles() wasn''t including the Permissions navigation property.\n\nFixed by using RolePermissionsSpec in GetRoles() to include permissions via Entity Framework Include statement, matching the behavior of GetRole(id).\n\nAlso updated the test to mock the specification-based Get method.\n\n✅ All 9 role tests passing\n✅ Backend builds successfully\n✅ Permissions now properly loaded for all roles in the list\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Group permissions by prefix in UI\n\nPermissions are now grouped by their resource type (the part before '':''):\n- Users (users:read, users:create, users:update, etc.)\n- Permissions (permissions:read, permissions:create, etc.)\n- Roles (roles:read, roles:create, etc.)\n- Blocks (blocks:read, blocks:create, etc.)\n- Company (company:read, company:create, etc.)\n\nEach group has a title and displays permissions in a grid layout within that group. Groups are sorted alphabetically for consistent display.\n\n✅ Frontend builds successfully\n✅ Improved UX - permissions are easier to find and organize\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* format:fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Add permission management storybook stories and improve codebase quality (#347)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Added story\n\n* fixed errors\n\n* errors fix\n\n* Initial scan completed - identified errors to fix\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix all TypeScript and formatting errors in RolesManagementBlock\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix all ESLint errors from CI build\n\n- Fix Math.random() impurity error by using React.useId() hook in Input component\n- Fix unescaped apostrophes in JSX text content\n- Fix unused variable errors by prefixing with underscore\n- Disable base no-unused-vars in favor of TypeScript version\n- Update Input test to work with useId generated IDs\n- All 159 tests passing, 0 errors (411 warnings)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix await-thenable errors in RolesManagementBlock.test.tsx\n\nRemove await keyword from act() calls with synchronous callbacks as they\nreturn non-Promises. This fixes all ''Unexpected await of a non-Promise''\nESLint errors in the test file.\n\n* Fix require-await warnings (94 fixed)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix all 105 prefer-nullish-coalescing ESLint warnings\n\nReplace || with ?? operator and if/assignment pattern with ??= where appropriate.\nThis provides safer null/undefined handling by only coalescing null/undefined values,\nnot falsy values like 0, '''', or false.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace || with ?? in 22 files across the dj-panel frontend\n- All 105 ESLint prefer-nullish-coalescing warnings resolved\n- All tests still passing\n\n* Fix import order warnings (4 fixed)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix simple warnings: no-return-await, no-non-null-assertion, prefer-optional-chain (3 fixed)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix remaining require-await in DynamicRoutes.tsx\n\n* Address code review feedback: fix Modal logic and simplify redundant ternary\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix 9 await-thenable errors in CompanyBlock test\n\nRemove await keywords before act() calls in CompanyBlock/index.test.tsx.\nThe act() function is not async, so awaiting it causes TypeScript errors.\nThis completes the require-await refactoring that was partially done earlier.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting issues in 6 files\n\nApply Prettier formatting to files modified during ESLint warning fixes.\nThis resolves the CI build failure caused by code style inconsistencies.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* enhance pipeline\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* format:fix\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* format:fix\n\n* fixup\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* removed not used tests (#351)\n\n* Expand atomic design system with core UI primitives (#349)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add new atomic components (Text, Link, Icon, Card, Badge, Divider) and organisms structure\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add tests for new atomic components and fix linting issues\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive README and fix TypeScript issues in new components\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive components README documentation\n\n* Add explanatory comment to organisms index about component location\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* removed files\n\n* format:fix\n\n* fixup\n\n* Fix test failures by adding React import to test files for JSX support\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add React import for Link component tests\n\n* Add React import for Badge test file\n\n* Update Card.test.tsx\n\n* Add React import for Divider test file\n\n* Add React import for Icon component tests\n\n* Add React import for JSX in Text.test.tsx\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* [WIP] Add pages and endpoint to manage user roles (#352)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add backend endpoints and frontend component for user role management\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix TypeScript type error in user-role-management-service\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address code review feedback - initialize DTO properties and improve error messages\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Delete Frontends/dj-panel/obj\\Debug/\\package.g.props\n\n* format:fix\n\n* Add comprehensive Storybook stories for UserRoleManagementBlock\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* install instead of clear install\n\n* delete lock file\n\n* updated gitignore\n\n* fixed story\n\n* Add user role management block to CMS seeder\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixed seeder\n\n* Fix seeder: use existing Roles Management Template for Users Management page\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add separate Users Management Template with user-role-management-block-ref\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Roles Management Template to use built-in block with no content\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add UsersManagement to TemplateType enum and wire up rendering\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make UsersManagement template use built-in block like RolesManagement\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix PRIMARY KEY violation when creating roles with permissions (#354)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix role creation by properly attaching existing permissions to DbContext\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Also fix UsersRepository Update to handle role relationships properly\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Complete fix for role creation error with code review and security check\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Prettier formatting issues in Button and Input components\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix UsersRepository Update to properly handle multiple role assignments\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix entity tracking conflict in UsersRepository Update method\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix HTTP 500 on GET identity/v1/Roles caused by circular reference and null navigation property (#358)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix HTTP 500 on identity/v1/Roles: return DTOs and fix DeleteRole null Users\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact and update gitignore\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Auto-refresh JWT token in background when user roles or role permissions change (#356)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* feat: auto-refresh JWT token when user roles or role permissions change\n\n- UpdateUserRoles now regenerates security stamp and invalidates cache after\n  successful role update, causing the user''s next request to get a 401 which\n  the frontend interceptor handles by calling RefreshToken\n- EditRole now finds all users assigned the edited role and invalidates their\n  security stamp caches so their tokens are refreshed with updated permissions\n- SecurityStampValidationTransform in gateway now skips stamp validation for\n  RefreshToken endpoint to avoid infinite 401 loops during token refresh\n- UsersService.RefreshToken now correctly fetches the user with roles/permissions\n  and generates a fresh token (removes broken RefreshTokenAsync call that\n  compared access token against stored refresh token, always failing)\n- Adds tests: UpdateUserRoles_RegeneratesSecurityStampAndInvalidatesCache and\n  EditRole_RegeneratesSecurityStampForAffectedUsers\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: remove accidentally committed Windows build artifact from git tracking\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: rebase onto releases/R2602 - bring in HTTP 500 roles fix\n\n- Add RoleWithUsersSpec for safe Users navigation include in DeleteRole\n- RolesService.GetRoles now returns List<GetRoleDTO> (caches DTOs to avoid circular refs)\n- RolesService.AddRole caches DTOs instead of entities in the All-roles cache\n- RolesService.DeleteRole uses RoleWithUsersSpec with null-safe Users check\n- RolesController.GetRolesV1 ProducesResponseType updated to IEnumerable<GetRoleDTO>\n- Remove unused ''using IdentityAPI.Entities'' from RolesController\n- RolesServiceTests updated: List<GetRoleDTO> cache mocks, ISpecification matchers for DeleteRole\n- .gitignore: add **/obj\\** pattern to block Windows build artifacts\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: correctly extract LoginResponseDTO from API response wrapper in refresh token interceptor\n\nThe v1UsersRefreshTokenList() endpoint returns LoginResponseDTOResponse\n(shape: { success, data: LoginResponseDTO, message, errors }).\nThe interceptor was casting response.data as LoginResponseDTO, so user/\naccessToken/refreshToken all resolved to undefined → null, clearing\nlocalStorage on every successful token refresh.\n\nFix: access response.data.data (the inner LoginResponseDTO) so the correct\nfields are read and localStorage is updated instead of cleared.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* format:fix\n\n* style: run prettier on Button.tsx and Input.tsx\n\nMerge interface extends clause onto a single line per prettier rules\n(printWidth: 80, singleQuote: true, trailingComma: all).\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* fix: reliably remove role from cache on deletion (#361)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* fix: only invalidate role cache when deletion succeeds, add cache invalidation tests\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: remove accidentally committed Windows build artifact from git tracking\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: use RemoveAsync for reliable role cache invalidation on deletion\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore: remove accidentally committed Windows build artifact from git tracking\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add integration tests for backend services (#362)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add integration tests for backend services\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact and update .gitignore\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix flaky Playwright tests (#363)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix flaky Playwright tests: reduce CI workers, improve waits and assertions\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptEdjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAax0QAIgjjNKuU6vDh69IA1i/JTJQ\n+j2tBqPRQu625L0hFucJqhCwOZ9Yz+HEdJam7vJVteJv3g3xDiUyu17qg9IHzDk+\nt1wKKVZAwnRK9nYiIpqn26LoMUQ5pndUGp+fgagz+uyEQNtiGi9EKJyY/hPG5A0p\nkf4Nk4J9pUY3o7AZ/ZJlF7z6TiepSfmrr406iZBNPC+UxqPXbUwWtXYOUUlKbip2\nKypKxymRbwTEhacj9Tt/sXbDkQk5OrQSahfUl+XHxfvUvlpLo9RdXjT8YIIyg7Jo\n/RbhPRteS6hsKangf9sHDn7eKVu0O9+xlexvyhxQH9CVTkbB/cmwqpF9uCRaZb22\n0g9V0hZkolLf+owJjtVv+++jIAwjZm199AsMflxKDNejhRHlt2T3uaPYcD/p3vbg\n1c2YHkWDnPMHUXD1+TqM8YXDTGFuwmHHKxx3jqyWz5cJ0lNIIGiJTIu/872BOrFC\n64zUFwlKyBlmxYuqh5yfDLazc8F3/wwIpizWrmJSTRagZ+EHrzyJQY24jtGbXzJ5\nmhPlY2hyr7zg7MIoXJ5sguzMygYBfnILfanq1RnvpSt0DcyEZ2G4mNFUVLQRDr18\n55ju509dQeCpPfWWuF4s9whcl0SIDuOhEl8IyF1IcFr/Xh30lP5/0xipctzDUpK/\nTIftJtvOXPM0S8MucO1w\n=zCxT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-13T17:20:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.git