ored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix singleton template blocks rendering \"No content loaded\" when CMS data is null (#321)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix profile page showing no content by rendering blocks with default props\n\nModified RenderTemplate.tsx to always render singleton blocks (Login, ForgotPassword, ChangePassword, Profile) even when Strapi returns null/empty data. Components have default props that will be used when no CMS data is configured.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* format:fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Consolidate all Strapi utilities into single RefBlockRenderer file (#317)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Remove strapiDocId.ts and consolidate getDocId function\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Also consolidate FIELD_BY_REF constant to eliminate duplication\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* map:api\n\n* Fix imports to use transformStrapiBlocks instead of non-existent mapStrapiContentToFrontend\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Merge transformStrapiBlocks logic into RefBlockRenderer for unified handling\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Improve isPopulated check to verify actual data content\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Optimize isPopulated with useMemo and fix dependency array\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use block as dependency instead of derived relObj to prevent stale closures\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Merge transformStrapiBlocks.ts into RefBlockRenderer.tsx and delete file\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix 404 error for profile block by passing empty query object to singleton getters\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Revert singleton getters to call without parameters - the original code was correct\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n* format:fix\n\n* fixup\n\n* format:fix\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Colocate types with components: remove content-blocks.ts and navigation-item.ts (#325)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Refactor content-blocks.ts to use generic type system for better extensibility\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive documentation for new content-blocks type system\n\n* Address code review feedback: improve documentation and type safety guidance\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n* Remove content-blocks.ts and move types to specific render files\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix TemplateEntity type incompatibility by removing Partial<Template> extension\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* format:fix\n\n* Fix TemplateEntity type to accept Template from Strapi service\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup on template\n\n* Fix marked.parse to use synchronous mode for TypeScript compatibility\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* format:fix\n\n* Unify NavigationItem and MenuNavigationItem types in DynamicRoutes.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Jest configuration to transform ES modules from marked and dompurify packages\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Add distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry and Grafana Tempo (#336)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry and Tempo\n\n- Added Tempo service to docker-compose for distributed tracing backend\n- Configured Tempo datasource in Grafana with trace-to-logs correlation\n- Added OpenTelemetry packages to Shared.csproj\n- Implemented OpenTelemetry instrumentation in ServicesBuilder.cs with ASP.NET Core, HttpClient, and SqlClient\n- Created TraceContextEnricher to include trace IDs in logs\n- Updated all backend services with TEMPO and LOKI environment variables\n- Connected all backend services to logging_net network for Tempo access\n- Configured W3C Trace Context propagation in API Gateway reverse proxy\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Enhance Grafana dashboard with trace visualization and fix build issues\n\n- Added 3 new panels to dashboard: Distributed Traces, Service Dependency Graph, and Service-to-Service Request Rate\n- Fixed OpenTelemetry vulnerability by upgrading to OpenTelemetry.Api 1.11.2\n- Updated OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http to 1.11.0\n- Removed non-existent SetDbStatementForStoredProcedure option\n- Verified build succeeds for Shared and IdentityAPI projects\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address code review feedback\n\n- Fixed TraceContextEnricher to only add ParentId for non-root spans\n- Changed string comparisons to case-insensitive for health check filtering\n- Made SQL statement logging conditional (only in development environments)\n- Fixed Grafana Loki regex to match actual log format (TraceId vs trace_id)\n- Reduced trace-to-logs time shift from 1h to 5m for better correlation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove redundant HTTP enrichment tags\n\n- Removed custom http.request.method and http.response.status_code tags as they are already captured by default OpenTelemetry HTTP instrumentation\n- Follows OpenTelemetry semantic conventions\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove backup file\n\n* Remove backup file from repository\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix react-router security vulnerabilities\n\n- Upgraded react-router and react-router-dom to 7.12.0\n- Resolved GHSA-h5cw-625j-3rxh (CSRF issue)\n- Resolved GHSA-2w69-qvjg-hvjx (XSS via Open Redirects)\n- Resolved GHSA-8v8x-cx79-35w7 (SSR XSS)\n- Verified build succeeds after update\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove build artifact from repository\n\nDeleted Frontends/dj-panel/obj\\Debug/\\package.g.props - this file is a build artifact that should not be in version control and is already covered by .gitignore\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Redis infinite memory usage and Grafana infinity display in dev on TrueNAS (#338)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix Redis infinite memory usage by adding maxmemory limits and eviction policy\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry and Grafana Tempo (#336)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry and Tempo\n\n- Added Tempo service to docker-compose for distributed tracing backend\n- Configured Tempo datasource in Grafana with trace-to-logs correlation\n- Added OpenTelemetry packages to Shared.csproj\n- Implemented OpenTelemetry instrumentation in ServicesBuilder.cs with ASP.NET Core, HttpClient, and SqlClient\n- Created TraceContextEnricher to include trace IDs in logs\n- Updated all backend services with TEMPO and LOKI environment variables\n- Connected all backend services to logging_net network for Tempo access\n- Configured W3C Trace Context propagation in API Gateway reverse proxy\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Enhance Grafana dashboard with trace visualization and fix build issues\n\n- Added 3 new panels to dashboard: Distributed Traces, Service Dependency Graph, and Service-to-Service Request Rate\n- Fixed OpenTelemetry vulnerability by upgrading to OpenTelemetry.Api 1.11.2\n- Updated OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http to 1.11.0\n- Removed non-existent SetDbStatementForStoredProcedure option\n- Verified build succeeds for Shared and IdentityAPI projects\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address code review feedback\n\n- Fixed TraceContextEnricher to only add ParentId for non-root spans\n- Changed string comparisons to case-insensitive for health check filtering\n- Made SQL statement logging conditional (only in development environments)\n- Fixed Grafana Loki regex to match actual log format (TraceId vs trace_id)\n- Reduced trace-to-logs time shift from 1h to 5m for better correlation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove redundant HTTP enrichment tags\n\n- Removed custom http.request.method and http.response.status_code tags as they are already captured by default OpenTelemetry HTTP instrumentation\n- Follows OpenTelemetry semantic conventions\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove backup file\n\n* Remove backup file from repository\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix react-router security vulnerabilities\n\n- Upgraded react-router and react-router-dom to 7.12.0\n- Resolved GHSA-h5cw-625j-3rxh (CSRF issue)\n- Resolved GHSA-2w69-qvjg-hvjx (XSS via Open Redirects)\n- Resolved GHSA-8v8x-cx79-35w7 (SSR XSS)\n- Verified build succeeds after update\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove build artifact from repository\n\nDeleted Frontends/dj-panel/obj\\Debug/\\package.g.props - this file is a build artifact that should not be in version control and is already covered by .gitignore\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix Grafana Redis memory usage gauge to prevent infinity display\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add company details page with user management, onboarding flow, membership-based modal, automatic owner assignment, permission-based authorization, secure service-to-service authentication, automatic SuperOwner permission management, Identity database ... (#331)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add backend CompanyAPI endpoints and services\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@u