ose configuration for sub-3-minute deployments (#258)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Optimize Dockerfiles - improve caching, reduce layers, optimize health checks\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add resource limits and health checks to docker-compose services\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive Docker optimization summary documentation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address code review feedback - improve comments and documentation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add Docker optimization quick reference guide\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix lint warning and remove duplicate healthchecks from compose file\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove duplicate healthchecks from docker-compose (already in Dockerfiles)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix NuGet package availability in dotnet.Dockerfile (#260)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Remove cache mount from dotnet restore to fix MessagePackAnalyzer not found error\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix React Dockerfile build failure: align Node.js versions to v22 LTS (#262)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix Node.js version mismatch: downgrade from node:25 to node:22 LTS\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add documentation explaining why SECURE_KEY/JWT_TOKEN are not secrets\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Improve documentation consistency for configuration identifiers\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Correct documentation: acknowledge secrets are in GitHub but exposed in client bundle\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix React Dockerfile webpack-cli installation: add --include=dev flag for NODE_ENV=production (#264)\n\n* Fix React Dockerfile build failure: align Node.js versions to v22 LTS (#262)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix Node.js version mismatch: downgrade from node:25 to node:22 LTS\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add documentation explaining why SECURE_KEY/JWT_TOKEN are not secrets\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Improve documentation consistency for configuration identifiers\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Correct documentation: acknowledge secrets are in GitHub but exposed in client bundle\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix React Dockerfile webpack-cli installation issue\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Re-apply webpack-cli fix after merge conflict resolution\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix webpack-cli installation: add --include=dev flag for NODE_ENV=production\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Implement comprehensive backup/restore and automatic rollback for deployment pipeline (#254)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add data backup, service stop, and automatic rollback with data restoration\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive documentation for build infrastructure pipeline\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix step order in workflows - prepare scripts before using them\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add final implementation summary for build infrastructure pipeline rewrite\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove invalid ''script_stop'' parameter from appleboy/ssh-action\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix shellcheck lint errors and improve error handling\n\n- Fix SC2086: Quote variables in GITHUB_OUTPUT redirects\n- Fix SC2129: Use command grouping for multiple redirects\n- Fix misleading comments: Change \"base64\" to \"heredoc\"\n- Synchronize timestamps between compose and data backups\n- Capture and log tar errors instead of redirecting to /dev/null\n- Verify restored files exist after extraction\n- Update backup script to accept optional timestamp parameter\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Track skipped volumes separately in backup statistics\n\n- Return distinct exit codes (2, 3) for skipped volumes\n- Add skipped_count tracking in backup loop\n- Include skipped volumes in summary output\n- Provide accurate statistics distinguishing successful, skipped, and failed backups\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* update to use DbContextFactory\n\n* Fix Docker tag determination to use triggering workflow''s branch\n\nOverride GITHUB_REF for determine-docker-tag step when triggered by workflow_run.\nThis ensures Docker tags are generated based on the Build Artifacts workflow''s\nbranch, not the Build Infrastructure workflow''s branch, allowing proper image\nmatching between build and deployment phases.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update tests\n\n* Add debug output and fix concurrency group for workflow_run triggers\n\n- Fix concurrency group to use triggering workflow''s branch when triggered by workflow_run\n- Add debug step to display actual branch/commit being used for deployment\n- Shows triggering workflow information when triggered by workflow_run\n- Helps diagnose branch mismatch issues between build and deployment\n\nThe GitHub UI may show the workflow running from the branch where the workflow\nfile exists (e.g., releases/R2512), but the actual code checkout uses the\ntriggering workflow''s branch and commit (e.g., copilot/rewrite-build-pipeline).\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix dev environment URL format from dash to dot separator\n\nChange maintenance page route pattern from dev-djbeatblaster.com to dev.djbeatblaster.com.\nThis ensures consistency with the domain pattern used in Cloudflare Tunnel ingress\nand DNS record creation, where environment prefix uses dot notation (e.g., dev.domain.com).\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use latest Docker tags for deployment to improve TrueNAS load times\n\nSwitch from commit-based tags to latest tags (dev-latest/prod-latest) in:\n- Docker image verification check\n- Compose file generation\n- Deployment summary\n\nThis allows TrueNAS to pull potentially cached images faster, reducing\ndeployment timeout issues. Commit-based tags are still created by Build\nArtifacts workflow and remain available for rollback purposes.\n\nBenefits:\n- Faster image pulls with latest tags (may be cached)\n- Reduced TrueNAS load time during deployment\n- Commit-based tags preserved for precise rollback operations\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Increase health check timeout to 60 minutes and create Docker optimization issue template\n\nTemporary fix for deployment timeouts:\n- Increased health check timeout from 30 to 60 minutes (360 checks)\n- Adjusted max_health_checks from 1000 to 360 for clearer timing\n- Updated timeout comment and error message\n\nLong-term solution:\n- Created comprehensive issue template for Docker image optimization\n- Documented root causes: large images, slow startups, missing optimizations\n- Proposed solutions for frontend and Strapi services\n- Included implementation plan, success criteria, and metrics tracking\n- Added references to Docker best practices and resources\n\nThis provides immediate relief from timeout errors while establishing a clear\npath forward for addressing the underlying performance issues.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Move maintenance page before stopping services\n\nChanges job execution order to match requirements:\n1. Setup build\n2. Backup compose state\n3. Backup data volumes\n4. Enable maintenance page (MOVED: now before stop_services)\n5. Stop services (now waits for maintenance page)\n6. Calculate ports\n7. Generate compose\n8. Deploy\n9. Update Cloudflare\n\nImplementation details:\n- Changed enable_maintenance_page dependencies from [generate_compose, setup, test_compose] to [setup, backup_data_volumes]\n- Changed stop_services dependencies from [setup, backup_data_volumes] to [setup, backup_data_volumes, enable_maintenance_page]\n- Switched maintenance page to use predefined service list (dj-panel, strapi-cms) instead of dynamic external_map_json\n- This ensures users see maintenance page BEFORE services stop, improving UX\n\nThe order now correctly implements: maintenance ON → services STOP → deploy → maintenance OFF\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix: Move compose generation before maintenance page and use external_map\n\nProperly implement the requested workflow order and dynamic service detection:\n\n1. Job Dependencies Fixed:\n   - enable_maintenance_page now depends on [setup, generate_and_upload_truenas_compose_file]\n   - This ensures compose is generated BEFORE maintenance page is enabled\n\n2. Dynamic Service Detection:\n   - Maintenance page now uses external_map_json from compose generation output\n   - Extracts actual service names using: jq -r ''keys[]''\n   - Removes hardcoded EXTERNAL_SERVICES=\"dj-panel strapi-cms\"\n   - Routes are created only for services actually in the deployment\n\nWorkflow order is now correct:\nSetup → Backup → Generate Compose → Enable Maintenance (with external_map) → Stop Services → Deploy\n\nThis ensures:\n- Compose file is created first with all service configurations\n- Maintenance page knows exactly which services need routes\n- No hardcoded service lists - uses real deployment data\n- Better reliability and accuracy\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix cyclic dependency: Move port calculation before service shutdown\n\nBreak the circular dependency chain by changing get_truenas_ports to depend on\nbackup_data_volumes instead of stop_services.\n\nThe cycle was:\nstop_services → enable_maintenance_page → generate_compose →\ncalculate_ports → get_ports → stop_services (CYCLE!)\n\nFixed workflow order:\n1. Setup\n2. Backup compose & data\n3. Get TrueNAS ports (parallel with backups, no longer waits for service stop)\n4. Calculate unused ports\n5. Generate compose file (uses calculated ports)\n6. Enable maintenance page (uses external_map from compose)\n7. Stop services (now properly sequenced after maintenance is enabled)\n8. Deploy services\n\nBenefits:\n- Eliminates cyclic dependency error\n- Port calculation happens earlier, improving parallelization\n- Services stop only after maintenance page is active\n- Compose generation uses fresh port data without requiring service shutdown\n- Logical workflow sequence maintained\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Fix TrueNAS deployment timeout by optimizing dependencies, healthchecks, and migrating to official images (#266)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Fix deployment timeout by adding command_timeout to SSH action\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update documentation to reflect correct 60-minute deployment timeout\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add healthchecks to all infrastructure and backend services to fix timeout\n\nAdded proper healthcheck configurations to prevent Docker Compose from waiting indefinitely:\n- Infrastructure: mongodb, redis, rabbitmq, sqlserver, strapi_db, loki\n- Backend services: apigateway, identity_be, music_be, gear_be, documents_be, brand_be, mailing_be, party_be\n- CMS: strapi\n\nTotal: 15 healthcheck configurations added to resolve TrueNAS timeout issue\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Revert: Remove redundant healthchecks from compose file\n\nHealthchecks are already properly defined in Dockerfiles. The compose file healthchecks I added were redundant and would override the Dockerfile definitions.\n\nThe actual timeout issue is likely due to cumulative healthcheck times across the 38 service dependencies.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Optimize deployment: relax monitoring service dependencies\n\nPhase 1 implementation to reduce startup time by allowing monitoring services to start in parallel without waiting for healthchecks.\n\nChanges (service_healthy → service_started):\n- sqlserver-exporter (no longer waits for sqlserver healthy)\n- mongodb-exporter (no longer waits for mongodb healthy)\n- postgres-exporter (no longer waits for strapi_db healthy)\n- redis-exporter (no longer waits for redis healthy)\n- grafana (no longer waits for loki/prometheus healthy)\n- promtail (no longer waits for loki healthy)\n\nImpact:\n- 6 services now use service_started (was 0)\n- 32 services still use service_healthy (critical path)\n- Estimated reduction: 2-3 minutes from theoretical startup time\n- Risk: Very low (monitoring services are non-critical)\n\nAnalysis document added: DEPLOYMENT_TIMEOUT_ANALYSIS.md\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Phase 2: Aggressively optimize healthcheck timings for faster deployment\n\nReduced healthcheck start periods and intervals across all critical path services to achieve ~40% faster startup time.\n\nChanges to healthcheck configurations:\n\nInfrastructure (Level 0):\n- mongodb.Dockerfile: start-period 90s→45s, interval 30s→15s\n- sqlserver.Dockerfile: start-period 60s→40s, interval 30s→15s\n- postgres.Dockerfile: start-period 60s→40s, interval 30s→15s\n- rabbitmq.Dockerfile: start-period 60s→40s, interval 30s→15s\n- redis.Dockerfile: start-period 30s→20s, interval 30s→10s\n\nApplication (Level 1):\n- strapi.Dockerfile: start-period 120s→60s, interval 30s→15s\n- dotnet.Dockerfile: start-period 60s→40s, interval 30s→15s (affects 8 backend services + apigateway)\n\nImpact:\n- Theoretical startup: 310s→185s (~3 minutes, 40% faster)\n- Realistic startup: 8-12min→5-7min (estimated with retries)\n- More frequent checks (15s intervals) = faster failure detection\n- All timings still conservative for reliability\n\nCombined with Phase 1 (relaxed monitoring deps), total expected improvement: 4-5 minutes faster deployment.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix TrueNAS deployment timeout by optimizing dependencies and healthcheck timings\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Phase 2.5A: Migrate 7 services to official Docker images with compose-based config\n\nMigrated infrastructure services to use official images directly, eliminating custom Dockerfiles and build time. Moved healthchecks and environment variables to docker-compose file for easier maintenance.\n\nServices migrated to official images:\n1. redis: redis:8-alpine (was custom build)\n2. sqlserver: mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest (was custom build)\n3. strapi_db (postgres): postgres:18 (was custom build)\n4. sqlserver-exporter: awaragi/prometheus-mssql-exporter:latest\n5. mongodb-exporter: percona/mongodb_exporter:0.40\n6. postgres-exporter: prometheuscommunity/postgres-exporter:latest\n7. redis-exporter: oliver006/redis_exporter:latest\n\nChanges to docker-compose file:\n- Replaced build: directives with image: directives\n- Added environment: blocks with necessary env vars\n- Added healthcheck: blocks (previously in Dockerfiles)\n- Added command: overrides where needed (redis, mongodb-exporter)\n- Added user: root where needed (redis, sqlserver)\n\nChanges to generate script:\n- Added logic to detect and preserve image: directives\n- Auto-detect port function for services without dockerfiles\n- No longer warns about missing dockerfiles for official images\n\nImpact:\n- Eliminates build time for 7 services (~1-3 minutes saved per deploy)\n- Reduces custom Dockerfiles from 14 → 7 (50% reduction)\n- Easier to maintain - healthchecks and config in one place\n- Can update images by just changing tag in compose file\n\nNote: This follows the new requirement to move healthchecks and env vars to docker-compose for simpler management.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove 7 unused Dockerfiles after Phase 2.5A migration\n\nRemoved Dockerfiles that are no longer needed after migrating to official images:\n- Docker/infra/redis.Dockerfile\n- Docker/infra/sqlserver.Dockerfile\n- Docker/infra/postgres.Dockerfile\n- Docker/infra/redis-exporter.Dockerfile\n- Docker/infra/mongodb-exporter.Dockerfile\n- Docker/infra/postgres-exporter.Dockerfile\n- Docker/infra/sqlserver-exporter.Dockerfile\n\nThese services now use official images with configuration in docker-compose.yml.\n\nRemaining custom Dockerfiles (7):\n- grafana.Dockerfile (complex config)\n- loki.Dockerfile (custom config)\n- mongodb.Dockerfile (needs init script)\n- prometheus.Dockerfile (custom config)\n- promtail.Dockerfile (custom config)\n- rabbitmq.Dockerfile (needs cookie fix)\n- strapi.Dockerfile (custom build - candidate for future Phase 2.5B)\n\nTotal reduction: 14 → 7 Dockerfiles (50% fewer files to maintain)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update CI build pipeline to remove deleted infrastructure Dockerfiles\n\nRemoved 7 services from build_infrastructure_images matrix that no longer need custom builds:\n- postgres (now uses postgres:18 official image)\n- redis (now uses redis:8-alpine official image)\n- sqlserver (now uses mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest)\n- sqlserver-exporter (now uses awaragi/prometheus-mssql-exporter:latest)\n- mongodb-exporter (now uses percona/mongodb_exporter:0.40)\n- postgres-exporter (now uses prometheuscommunity/postgres-exporter:latest)\n- redis-exporter (now uses oliver006/redis_exporter:latest)\n\nThese services are now configured directly in docker-compose.yml with official images.\n\nRemaining infrastructure builds (7):\n- mongodb (needs init script)\n- rabbitmq (needs cookie fix)\n- strapi (custom CMS build)\n- loki (custom logging config)\n- promtail (custom log collection)\n- grafana (complex datasource config)\n- prometheus (custom scrape config)\n\nImpact:\n- Build pipeline now builds 14 → 7 infrastructure images (50% fewer)\n- Eliminates 1-3 minutes from CI pipeline build time\n- Reduces GHCR storage and bandwidth usage\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix deployment verification to exclude official images\n\nUpdated deployment verification script to only check custom-built images:\n- Removed sqlserver from image verification list (now uses mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest)\n- Added comment clarifying that official images (redis, postgres, sqlserver, exporters) are not checked\n- These official images are pulled directly from Docker Hub / Microsoft registry\n\nRemaining custom-built images checked:\n- djhostgateway (service)\n- companyapi (service)\n- dj-panel (frontend)\n- mongodb (infrastructure - needs init script)\n\nThis fixes the deployment failure:\n\"❌ Missing: ghcr.io/psptorchinim/micros/infra/sqlserver:dev-latest\"\n\nThe sqlserver image no longer exists in GHCR because it now uses the official Microsoft image directly.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n* Fix storybook image name generation in compose file\n\nThe generate script was incorrectly using the MICROFRONTEND_NAME argument (dj-panel) for storybook instead of the dockerfile base name (storybook).\n\nUpdated dockerfile_to_image function to:\n- Check if dockerfile base name is \"storybook\"\n- Use \"storybook\" directly for the image name instead of MICROFRONTEND_NAME\n- Generates: ghcr.io/.../frontends/storybook:dev-latest (correct)\n- Previously: ghcr.io/.../frontends/dj-panel:dev-latest (incorrect)\n\nThis ensures storybook service uses its own dedicated image instead of the dj-panel frontend image.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix SQL Server exporter authentication issue\n\nChanged sqlserver-exporter USERNAME from variable ${DATABASE_USER_SQLSERVER} to hardcoded ''sa'' to match SQL Server configuration.\n\nThe SQL Server official image only has the ''sa'' user enabled by default with password set via MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD. The exporter was trying to use DATABASE_USER_SQLSERVER (which might be a different username or misconfigured), causing authentication failures:\n\n\"Login failed for user ''sa''. Reason: Password did not match\"\n\nThis fix ensures the exporter uses the correct ''sa'' username that SQL Server expects.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix SQL Server authentication for all backend services\n\nChanged all backend services to use ''sa'' username instead of ${DATABASE_USER_SQLSERVER} variable for SQL Server connections.\n\nThe SQL Server official image (mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest) only creates the ''sa'' user by default with the password from MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD. Application services were trying to connect with DATABASE_USER_SQLSERVER which might not exist, causing authentication failures:\n\n\"Login failed for user ''sa''. Reason: Password did not match\"\n\nUpdated 8 backend services:\n- apigateway (DJHostGateway)\n- identity-be (IdentityAPI)\n- music-be (MusicAPI)\n- gear-be (EquipmentAPI)\n- documents-be (DocumentsAPI)\n- companyapi (CompanyAPI)\n- mailing-be (MailingAPI)\n- party-be (PartyAPI)\n\nAll services now use ASPNETCORE_DATABASE_USER_SQLSERVER=sa with password from DATABASE_PASSWORD_SQLSERVER GitHub secret.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix SQL Server healthcheck to use correct password variable\n\nThe healthcheck was using $MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD which wasn''t available as an environment variable during healthcheck execution. Changed to use ${DATABASE_PASSWORD_SQLSERVER} directly, which is the GitHub secret that contains the actual password.\n\nAlso added DATABASE_PASSWORD_SQLSERVER to the environment block so it''s available for the healthcheck command.\n\nThis should resolve the \"Login failed for user ''sa''. Reason: Password did not match\" error that was occurring during SQL Server healthcheck execution.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix storybook image name and postgres healthcheck variables\n\nFixed two deployment issues:\n\n1. **Storybook image name**:\n   - CI builds storybook as `storybook-dj-panel` (service-name in workflow uses \"storybook-${{ matrix.image.name }}\")\n   - Generate script now correctly uses the full service name for storybook services (e.g., storybook-dj-panel)\n   - Image: ghcr.io/.../frontends/storybook-dj-panel:dev-latest ✅\n\n2. **Postgres healthcheck environment variables**:\n   - Changed from $POSTGRES_USER/$POSTGRES_DB to ${CMS_DATABASE_USERNAME}/${CMS_DATABASE_NAME}\n   - These match the actual environment variables defined in the compose file\n   - Fixes: \"The POSTGRES_USER variable is not set\" warning\n\nThis resolves the TrueNAS error: \"Head ghcr.io/.../frontends/storybook/manifests/dev-latest: denied\" (image doesn''t exist)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Exclude database services from external Cloudflare tunnel access\n\nUpdated generate-compose-file.sh to assign internal ports (not publicly exposed) to infrastructure database services when using official images:\n- strapi_db (PostgreSQL)\n- redis\n- sqlserver\n- mongodb_container\n- rabbitmq\n\nThese services should only be accessible internally within the Docker network, not via public Cloudflare tunnel.\n\n**Before:** These services were assigned external ports (50004, 50007, 50008) and exposed via Cloudflare\n**After:** These services get internal ports (40000-49999) and are NOT exposed publicly\n\nOnly application services (apigateway, dj-panel, strapi, grafana, storybook) should be publicly accessible.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n* Update dj-panel-composer.yml\n\n* fixup\n\n* removed issue template\n\n* fixup\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Remove dead interceptor code causing runtime errors in API client (#267)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Remove dead code: fix microservicesClient undefined reference and invalid Api.prototype checks\n\nResolved code review comments by removing dead interceptor code that would never execute:\n1. Lines 29-40 in api.ts referenced undefined microservicesClient variable\n2. Lines 745-755 in all apiMap.ts files checked Api.prototype.instance which is always false\n\nThe secure_key interceptor is already properly handled in UnifiedApi class constructor.\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Removed MD files for future update of documentation\n\n* Remove unused variables and imports flagged by code review (#269)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Remove unused variables and imports from test files and API client\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Upgrade Strapi to v5.33.0 (#268)\n\n* [WIP] Fix error CS5001 for missing static Main method (#271)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add missing Program.cs to CompanyAPI project\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Implement security stamp for forced logout on password change with Strapi CMS integration (#273)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Add security stamp fields and core functionality\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive tests for security stamp functionality\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address code review feedback - improve error handling and security\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add comprehensive documentation for security stamp feature\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix YARP transform to validate all requests except ValidateSecurityStamp endpoint\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact file\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Reorder validation checks - skip if no JWT first, then check endpoint\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix CodeQL security issues - remove user input from logs and improve exception handling\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* updated packages\n\n* added migrations\n\n* Fix database migrations to use MigrateAsync and fix package compatibility\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix nullable reference type warnings in Shared project\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Added migrations\n\n* Add clean build instructions to resolve Swashbuckle version downgrade issue\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add Docker-specific rebuild instructions and helper script for TrueNAS deployments\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Docker build to use --no-cache for NuGet restore to prevent Swashbuckle version conflicts\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixed to latest versions\n\n* removed not needed files\n\n* Replace incompatible Treyt.Yarp.ReverseProxy.Swagger with secure custom implementation (#279)\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Initial plan for fixing Swagger and Reverse Proxy compatibility\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Replace incompatible Treyt.Yarp.ReverseProxy.Swagger with custom implementation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Address code review feedback - use ConfigureAwait(false) to reduce deadlock risk\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove accidentally committed build artifact (obj/Debug/package.g.props)\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add SSRF protection and resource limits to ReverseProxyDocumentFilter\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Refactor SSRF protection - extract helper method and use named constants\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Replace incompatible Treyt.Yarp.ReverseProxy.Swagger with secure custom implementation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove build artifact and update .gitignore to prevent re-adding\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove build artifact obj/Debug/package.g.props from repository\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup on determining env\n\n* Fix race condition in SeedPermissions causing duplicate key violations\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make database seeding fully idempotent to prevent duplicate key violations\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix role seeding to prevent EF Core from treating existing permissions as new entities\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Simplify role seeding using repository Update method instead of manual context management\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fixup\n\n* Fix duplicate key violation in role seeding by handling concurrent inserts gracefully\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Handle concurrent role insert exceptions properly by catching and recovering gracefully\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix duplicate key violation in SeedUsers by creating user first then assigning roles separately\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Revert \"Handle concurrent role insert exceptions properly by catching and recovering gracefully\"\n\nThis reverts commit cd0abca7e89e039cdcddc1b644e52dccd8f96c3d.\n\n* Add Strapi CMS proxy through API Gateway for automatic security stamp validation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add Strapi Swagger/OpenAPI specification to API Gateway schema discovery\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* added env variables\n\n* Fix Strapi route to preserve /api prefix when proxying requests\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* moved strapi to be hidden after API Gateway\n\n* fixup on populate\n\n* audit fix\n\n* Route Strapi API calls through microservices gateway, consolidate type definitions, simplify gateway routing, add Redis-free DevelopmentLocal support, and fix security vulnerabilities ([#281](https://github.com/PSPTorchinim/micros/issues/281))\n\n* Initial plan\n\n* Replace strapiAPI with microservicesClient-based implementation\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix test mocks to use strapi-microservice\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Translate Polish comments to English for consistency\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Strapi OpenAPI configuration to remove invalid properties\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove map-strapi script and strapiMap, use API gateway types instead\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix NullReferenceException in ReverseProxyDocumentFilter for null collections\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Refactor StrapiService to use static methods like UsersService\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* renamed StrapiService file to proper convention\n\n* Add StrapiService to ServicesContext and fix remaining strapiAPI references\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix type conversion error in ReverseProxyDocumentFilter dictionary initialization\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Tags collection type from List to HashSet for ISet compatibility\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix Strapi API Gateway routing to match generated client paths\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Skip Redis configuration when environment is DevelopmentLocal\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Refactor BuildBasicServices to simplify conditional logic\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove /api from microservice gateway routes to simplify Swagger paths\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* map:api\n\n* Strip /api prefix from backend Swagger paths when merging to gateway\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove /api prefix from BaseController route and revert Swagger path stripping\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove /api path transforms from microservice gateway routes\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add NoOpCacheService for DevelopmentLocal to bypass Redis caching\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* map:api\n\n* fixed links\n\n* format:fix\n\n* Fix npm security vulnerabilities by adding package overrides\n\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: PSPTorchinim <47593054+PSPTorchinim@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Hubert Troć <huberttroc@gmail.com>\n\n* Updated Strapi to latest version\n\n* remove audit on CMS\n\n* fixup on Strapi - allow to use Postgres\n\n* Add enhanced logging