rs/kushasahu7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushasahu7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushasahu7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushasahu7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushasahu7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kushasahu7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Starithm/Starithm-Home/commits/880776e04373550e079afb2e3246867699c9ee1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T06:29:10Z","email":"kusha.mil@gmail.com","name":"kushasahu7"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T06:29:10Z","email":"kusha.mil@gmail.com","name":"kushasahu7"},"message":"Ears: show the arrangement and the track''s real scale\n\nThe note ladder hard-coded \"D minor pent.\", which was wrong for every track\nnot actually in D minor. It now reads the scale the pipeline publishes,\nshortened for display because the ladder column is about 120px wide and a\nfull name like \"D suspended pentatonic\" wraps and pushes the rungs down.\n\nAdds a \"How it sounds\" block to the aside panel: the three instruments a\nlistener hears, the key, the acoustic space, and the one sentence the\narranger wrote about why it chose them. When the model made that choice\nrather than the fallback rule, the credits say the instruments were chosen\nby an AI model and that the data alone still decides every note. No model is\nnamed, matching how the poem is credited.\n\nTracks published before palettes existed carry no arrangement, so the block\nis simply absent and they render exactly as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5af1e8cf9c19d1952cdf0872a9fec65b102295d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Starithm/Starithm-Home/git/trees/5af1e8cf9c19d1952cdf0872a9fec65b102295d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Starithm/Starithm-Home/git/commits/8807