ion guidelines\n- Establish professional issue and PR management workflows\n\nBenefits:\n- Clear project identity as MFE component library/shell\n- Professional GitHub repository management\n- Automated CI/CD pipeline with quality gates\n- Standardized contribution process\n- Comprehensive documentation and setup guides\n\nMigration: Projects using this as a template should migrate to the new scoped package name","tree":{"sha":"902019e0f5d253eac2885f277cd90349aa86a3c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonmatum/react-mfe-shell/git/trees/902019e0f5d253eac2885f277cd90349aa86a3c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonmatum/react-mfe-shell/git/commits/61108cb3d568ccb0361ded4ca311b601d99e0098","verification":{"payload":"tree 902019e0f5d253eac2885f277cd90349aa86a3c5\nparent 82f92c5aa2eeeca1dddf64615a3b81f202cd53ae\nauthor Jonatan Mata <jonmatum@gmail.com> 1755285315 -0600\ncommitter Jonatan Mata <jonmatum@gmail.com> 1755285315 -0600\n\nfeat: rebrand as React MFE Shell and add comprehensive GitHub configuration\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Repository identity changed from template to production MFE shell\n\nRepository Identity Updates:\n- Rename from ''react-mfe-template'' to ''@jonmatum/react-mfe-shell''\n- Update package.json with scoped name and shell-focused description\n- Rebrand README.md to reflect MFE shell purpose (not template)\n- Update all documentation references from template to shell\n- Correct repository URLs throughout codebase\n\nGitHub Configuration Additions:\n- Add comprehensive CI workflow with testing, linting, and code analysis\n- Add automated release workflow with Release-Please integration\n- Add issue templates for bug reports and feature requests\n- Add pull request template with quality checklist\n- Add contributing guidelines with development workflow\n- Add repository setup documentation for maintainers\n- Configure Release-Please for automated version management\n\nQuality Improvements:\n- Add artifact uploads for code analysis and coverage rep