ng\n\n🎯 **Modal Footer Simplification**\n- Task Details Modal: Removed complex status buttons, kept only \"Mark as Completed\" for incomplete tasks\n- Create Task Modal: Removed redundant Cancel button, kept only primary Create action\n- Leveraged Modal''s built-in close functionality (ESC, backdrop) for cancellation\n- Cleaner UX with single, clear action per modal\n\n🏷️ **App Footer Enhancement with Branding**\n- Added TaskMaster Pro icon with checkmark circle design\n- Improved visual hierarchy: TaskMaster Pro → powered by → React MFE Shell\n- Used default badge variant for v6.2.0 version display (better theme compatibility)\n- Enhanced spacing and layout with proper app branding\n\n🎨 **Visual Design Improvements**\n- TaskMaster Icon: Professional checkmark circle representing task completion\n- Better text hierarchy: App name prominent, \"powered by\" secondary\n- Default badge variant: Theme-neutral styling that works in all modes\n- Consistent spacing with space-x-3 for better visual balance\n\n🔧 **UX Simplification Benefits**\n- Task Details: Only shows completion action when relevant (not for completed tasks)\n- Create Task: Single primary action reduces decision fatigue\n- Footer Branding: Clear app identity with technology attribution\n- Reduced Cognitive Load: Fewer buttons and clearer purpose\n\n📱 **Technical Improvements**\n- Added TaskMasterIcon component with checkmark circle SVG\n- Removed bg-surface-secondary from modal footers for cleaner appearance\n- Updated safelist with new footer classes (space-x-3, text-primary-600, font-semibold)\n- Proper Badge component usage with default variant\n\n🎯 **Modal UX Patterns**\n- Task Details: Show completion action only when actionable\n- Create Task: Focus on primary action, use built-in modal close for cancel\n- Consistent footer styling without background colors\n- Single full-width button for clear action hierarchy\n\nThis enhancement creates much cleaner modal interactions while establishing\nproper app 